<h2>Exercise 1: Box Model Visualization</h2>
        <div class="box-demo">Content (Background Color)</div>
        <div class="box-demo">Padding (Larger Click Area)</div>
        <div class="box-demo">Border (Visible Border)</div>
        <div class="box-demo">Margin (Space Between Boxes)</div>/* 1. Content: Just background color */
        .box-content {
            background-color: #e74c3c;
        }
        /* 2. Padding: Larger click/background area */
        .box-padding {
            background-color: #e67e22;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        /* 3. Border:Visible border around box */
        .box-border {
            background-color: #f1c40f;
            color: #2c3e50;
            padding: 20px;
            border: 4px solid #16a085;
        }
        /* 4. Margin: Creates space outside between boxes */
        .box-margin {
            background-color: #2ecc71;
            color: #2c3e50;
            padding: 20px;
            border: 4px solid #16a085;
            margin-top: 25px;/*--BOX MODEL VISUALIZATION--*/
        .exercise-1-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 15px;
        }
        .base-box {
            width: 250px;
            color: #ffffff;
        }
        /* Why it was 340px: Default box-sizing is content-box, so 300px + 20px left + 20px right = 340px */
        .broken-box {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            width: 300px;
            padding: 20px;
            border: none;
            background-color: #3498db;
            }
           .box-demo {
            width: 200px;
            background-color: #3498db;
            padding: 20px;
            border: 4px solid #2c3e50;
            margin: 15px;
            color: white;
        }  